Changes to Madeira's DXMT (third_party/madeira/dxmt). Applied by scripts/apply-patches.sh.

- src/airconv: no reassociation in shaders by default. LLVM turned a soft shadow's
  pow((36 - sum) / 36, 2.2) into an fma that left a tiny negative, so log2 gave NaN and the
  shadows went black. DXMT_PRECISE_MATH (1 all, 2 flags only, 4 math functions only) and
  DXMT_FAST_REASSOC=1 choose otherwise; the shader cache file is now *_win2.db
  (src/winemetal/unix/cache.c). The tessellation shader always uses the 4-argument barrier.
- src/dxmt/dxmt_dynamic.cpp: a dynamic buffer keeps as many renames as are in flight instead
  of trimming to 64, and walks its queue only with DXMT_DYN_STATS=1. Creating and freeing
  Metal buffers was 28% of a game's main thread.
- src/d3d9: an indexed draw stores only the index bytes it reads, not the whole buffer
  (MADEIRA_D3D9_INDEX_RANGE=0 restores the old refresh).
- src/dxmt/dxmt_mem_census: memory use by kind, logged now and then.

